p.src:
First comes switching cost: $\text{low switching cost for buyer}
\Rightarrow
\text{high churn risk for seller}.$ The lecture illustrates this with mobile carriers and gym memberships. Buyers like easy exit. Sellers dislike it because it creates turnover. Yet competitive pressure may force the seller to permit exactly that low-friction movement.

